[[2047,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The supply controlled by the ignition (INT) for the speedometer\nmodule \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               reaches pin 10 of connector A from the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99.</p><p>Pin 1 of connector A is earthed.</p><p>The &quot;warning lights test&quot; signal is sent:</p><ul><li>to the auxiliary instrument <strong>E20</strong> (pin 6) from pin\n4 of connector A;</li><li>to the check panel <strong>E30</strong> (pin 14) from pin 3 of connector\nA;</li><li>to the rev counter <strong>E15</strong> (pin 10 of connector B)\nfrom pin 3 of connector B.</li></ul>"]]